      "message": "It would be better if we do \u0027curr.batt.state_of_charge \u003c\u003d CONFIG_BATT_HOST_SHUTDOWN_PERCENTAGE\u0027 in a function:\n\n    bool battery_is_below_shutdown_threshold(int percent)\n    {\n        percent \u003c\u003d CONFIG_BATT_HOST_SHUTDOWN_PERCENTAGE);\n    }\n\nThat\u0027ll keep CONFIG_BATT_HOST_SHUTDOWN_PERCENTAGE in once place and prevent inconsistency from happening in terms of low-battery judgement. Also, it\u0027s easy to update the logic (e.g. to \u0027display_charge \u003c\u003d 0\u0027). \n\n\u003e the implementation is equivalent by translate the mapping from raw battery charge level to display charge level,\n\nIt\u0027s equivalent. However, ideally, we should use CONFIG_BATT_HOST_SHUTDOWN_PERCENTAGE only to calculate display_charge and the rest of the host related code should compare display_charge with 0.",
